            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and SAR studies of 3,6-disubstituted indazole derivatives as potent hepcidin production inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2148-2152</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(17)30305-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2017.03.056</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hepcidin has emerged as the central regulatory molecule of systemic iron homeostasis. Inhibition of hepcidin could be a strategy favorable to treating anemia of chronic disease (ACD). We report herein the synthesis and structure-activity relationships (SARs) of a series of indazole compounds as hepcidin production inhibitors. The optimization study of compound 1 led to a potent hepcidin production inhibitor 45, which showed serum hepcidin lowering effects in a mouse IL-6 induced acute inflammatory model.</AbstractText>
